                                    <component>cache</component>
                        <due></due>
                            <votes>0</votes>
                                    <watches>3</watches>
                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="14645078" author="agoncharuk" created="Tue, 28 Jul 2015 21:30:28 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The reason behind the failure (see GridNearGetFuture#map())&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;When data node is stopped, near entry becomes invalid because primary owner is changed&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;When &lt;tt&gt;get()&lt;/tt&gt; is called on near node, local variable &lt;tt&gt;entry&lt;/tt&gt; is first initialized with near entry, but &lt;tt&gt;innerGet()&lt;/tt&gt; returns &lt;tt&gt;null&lt;/tt&gt; because near entry is invalid&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Since offheap is enabled and node is client, &lt;tt&gt;dht.entryEx&lt;/tt&gt; throws invalid partition exception&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Local variable &lt;tt&gt;entry&lt;/tt&gt; remains initialized with near entry, however &lt;tt&gt;finally&lt;/tt&gt; block assumes that &lt;tt&gt;entry&lt;/tt&gt; is a DHT entry if not null&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="14645174" author="agoncharuk" created="Tue, 28 Jul 2015 23:11:22 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;There are two points that should be addressed:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Code that works with DHT entry should work with another local variable just to make it safer&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The DHT lookup should not be performed on a client node&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="14645176" author="agoncharuk" created="Tue, 28 Jul 2015 23:14:42 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Added patch with described fixes.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14646953" author="agoncharuk" created="Thu, 30 Jul 2015 00:11:07 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Yakov, can you review?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14650064" author="vkulichenko" created="Sat, 1 Aug 2015 00:25:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I looked at the changes - looks good for me.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14650074" author="agoncharuk" created="Sat, 1 Aug 2015 00:36:44 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The test added to the test suite. User who originally reported the issue confirmed that the fix works.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                    </comments>
